here are some things North Korea doesn't  have a human rights record to speak of  political or economic freedoms or enough  food to feed its citizens here's what  North Korea does have a nuclear weapons  program and an unpredictable young  leader whose finger is on the button our  North Korea's nuclear threats something  to fear are just saber rattling from an  isolated nation so here's the situation  at September 9th 2016 a 5.3 magnitude  earthquake was detected here it was  North Korea's fifth nuclear test in a  decade and a second this year it was  also the most powerful so far while  military experts suspect North Korea  exaggerates its achievements they agreed  his further detain of mounting a nuclear  warhead on a ballistic missile from Kim  il-sung to Kim jong-il to Kim jong-un  North Korea has been ruled by a family  of aggressive dictators since 1948 each  intent on a nuclear strategy that's deep  into the nation's isolation which is why  the u.s. currently has nearly 30,000  troops stationed in South Korea backed  with firepower such as Apache  helicopters have 16 fighters and nuclear  capable b-2 stealth bombers based in the  region now here's the argument this  could all just be a tactic North Korea  has a long history of escalating and  then de-escalating hostilities in order  to broker economic and diplomatic  concessions South Korea would support  from Japan and other nations will bear  most of the cost of providing North  Korea with fuel to make up for the  nuclear energy it is losing which leaves  the US and the world in a tricky  position most diplomatic situations call  for a carrot or stick approach  unfortunately with North Korea neither  the carrot in the form of aid nor the  stick in the form of sanctions has  worked with none of North Korea's  opponents willing to risk a military  confrontation over the nuclear issue the  most realistic options are ever stronger  sanctions were just to wait for the  downfall of the Kim dynasty neither is  ideal especially when Kim's erratic  behavior including executing his own  uncle is added to the mix
 

